          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دروغ گفتن (dorugh goftan) — \"to lie, to tell a lie\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بچه ها گاهی به پدر و مادرشان دروغ میگویند. bachchehâ gâhi be pedar-o mâdarashân dorugh miguyand. Children sometimes lie to their parents."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dorugh 'a lie' + goftan 'to say'; present stem gu-. The person lied to takes be. The opposite is râst goftan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dorugh is inherited: EtymDB traces it to Old Persian drauga, 'lie', and on to a Proto-Indo-European root for deceiving, and lists German Betrug, 'deceit', as a cousin (EtymDB). goftan, 'to say', is inherited too."
            }
          ]
        },
